discovery-path-30c1829e.conceptual_definition:
This formula provides an approximate relationship for the baryon number density (
        \(n_B\)
        ) generated in the early universe, particularly relevant in theories of baryogenesis such as electroweak baryogenesis. It quantifies how a fundamental asymmetry between matter and antimatter, characterized by CP violation (
        \(\Delta_{CP}\)
        ), is processed and amplified into a net baryon density by certain particle interactions (sphalerons) amidst the expansion of the universe.

